WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.517 --> 00:00:20.566
The small man cub sat in the circle with the wolf cubs.

2
00:00:21.847 --> 00:00:25.349
He was playing with some white pebbles that glowed in the moonlight.

3
00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.732
Father Wolf nudged Mowgli forward with his nose.

4
00:00:34.376 --> 00:00:36.257
"Look well, oh, wolves!"

5
00:00:36.798 --> 00:00:39.820
Akela cried, as he'd done with the other cubs.

6
00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:46.524
Before any wolves could respond, a muffled roar came from behind the rocks.

7
00:00:49.546 --> 00:00:50.867
It was Shere Khan.

8
00:00:50.887 --> 00:00:55.510
"The cub is mine!"

9
00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:57.311
the tiger growled.

10
00:00:57.331 --> 00:00:59.313
"Give him to me!"

11
00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.096
"Look well, oh, wolves!"

12
00:01:04.604 --> 00:01:05.505
Akela called.

13
00:01:05.525 --> 00:01:08.606
"Look well upon this cub!"

14
00:01:11.368 --> 00:01:15.530
The law of the jungle was that two wolves had to speak for the cub.

15
00:01:17.711 --> 00:01:20.553
This was how the pack accepted the wolf cubs.

16
00:01:20.573 --> 00:01:24.035
"Who will speak for this cub?"

17
00:01:24.655 --> 00:01:25.555
Akela called.

18
00:01:26.616 --> 00:01:29.798
Mother Wolf tensed, ready to defend Mowgli.

19
00:01:31.338 --> 00:01:33.900
Akela was still waiting for someone to speak.

20
00:01:34.944 --> 00:01:40.609
Besides the wolves in the pack, only one other animal was allowed at the pack council.

21
00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:48.915
It was Baloo, a sleepy brown bear who taught the wolf cubs the law of the jungle.

22
00:01:50.116 --> 00:01:56.541
Baloo ate only nuts, roots, and honey, so none of the other jungle creatures feared him.

23
00:01:57.582 --> 00:02:02.326
As Shere Khan stepped closer, the brown bear rose on his back legs.

24
00:02:03.127 --> 00:02:04.468
He grunted loudly.

25
00:02:05.148 --> 00:02:06.769
"I speak for the human cub.

26
00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.071
Let him run with the pack.

27
00:02:09.992 --> 00:02:12.874
I will teach him, as I teach the other cubs."

28
00:02:14.515 --> 00:02:17.037
"Who else will speak for the human cub?"

29
00:02:17.657 --> 00:02:18.618
Akela called.

30
00:02:19.999 --> 00:02:23.641
Just then a black shadow dropped down into the circle.

31
00:02:25.142 --> 00:02:27.664
It was Bagheera, the black panther.

32
00:02:28.685 --> 00:02:30.847
The wolves quickly backed away from him.

33
00:02:33.216 --> 00:02:35.137
"Akela, I have no right to be here."

34
00:02:36.158 --> 00:02:40.101
The black panther's voice was as soft as honey dripping from a tree.

35
00:02:40.121 --> 00:02:45.645
"But the law of the jungle says a cub's life may be bought.

36
00:02:46.085 --> 00:02:46.585
Am I right?"

37
00:02:46.605 --> 00:02:51.328
"Yes!" a few young wolves replied eagerly.

38
00:02:52.069 --> 00:02:54.470
The young wolves were always hungry.

39
00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:57.332
"Akela!" one wolf called.

40
00:02:57.352 --> 00:02:59.374
"Listen to Bagheera.

41
00:03:00.294 --> 00:03:02.276
The cub can be bought for a price.

42
00:03:02.992 --> 00:03:04.653
It is the law of the jungle."

43
00:03:06.174 --> 00:03:08.355
The black panther smiled gently.

44
00:03:08.375 --> 00:03:11.537
"I'd like to propose a deal.

45
00:03:12.137 --> 00:03:14.659
Baloo has already spoken for the boy.

46
00:03:15.779 --> 00:03:20.282
If the rest of you accept him, I will share some delicious food with you.

47
00:03:21.022 --> 00:03:23.103
It's a fat bull, freshly killed."

48
00:03:26.025 --> 00:03:27.606
Mother Wolf looked at Father.

49
00:03:27.626 --> 00:03:30.447
"Why is the panther speaking up for Mowgli?"

50
00:03:30.668 --> 00:03:31.168
she said.

51
00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:32.841
Father shrugged.

52
00:03:34.001 --> 00:03:37.103
The other wolves had gathered to discuss the situation.

53
00:03:37.123 --> 00:03:42.005
"The boy will die in the winter rains," one said.

54
00:03:42.025 --> 00:03:45.707
"He will burn in the sun," another added.

55
00:03:45.727 --> 00:03:48.809
"What harm can a little cub do?"

56
00:03:48.829 --> 00:03:51.270
"Come on.

57
00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.971
Let's let him run with the pack."

58
00:03:54.252 --> 00:03:57.454
Finally the wolves agreed to accept Mowgli.

59
00:03:58.274 --> 00:04:01.516
Mowgli sat calmly, playing with the white pebbles.

60
00:04:02.364 --> 00:04:05.525
Akela's cry rose as they each inspected him.

61
00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:08.986
"Look well—look well, wolves!"

62
00:04:10.426 --> 00:04:15.288
Soon the pack started down the hill to eat the meal promised by the panther.

63
00:04:16.888 --> 00:04:21.809
Akela, Bagheera, Baloo, and Mowgli's family stayed behind at the rock.

64
00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:26.250
With a furious roar, Shere Khan stalked away from them.

65
00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:31.612
"Roar all you want, tiger," Bagheera muttered.

66
00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.082
"I have a feeling about this man cub.

67
00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:41.205
One day Mowgli will make you roar for another reason, Shere Khan."

68
00:04:42.626 --> 00:04:46.008
Akela turned to Mother and Father Wolf with a smile.

69
00:04:46.028 --> 00:04:49.170
"Humans are very wise.

70
00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:53.172
Perhaps your man cub can help our pack in some way."

71
00:04:54.493 --> 00:04:56.594
Mowgli's parents nodded their thanks.

72
00:04:57.354 --> 00:04:59.736
Then Father Wolf turned to the bear.

73
00:05:01.576 --> 00:05:03.940
"And thank you for your help today, Baloo.

74
00:05:05.021 --> 00:05:08.226
Please begin training little Mowgli as soon as possible.

75
00:05:09.588 --> 00:05:11.591
He must learn how to be a wolf."
